# requires: arch=arm64 -threaded

# pKVM memslot reject A (dirty/readonly flags on a protected VM). Register a memslot with
# KVM_MEM_LOG_DIRTY_PAGES (0x1) on a protected VM. kvm_arch_prepare_memory_region rejects a slot
# whose flags carry LOG_DIRTY/READONLY as soon as pkvm.enabled is set -> -EPERM, WITHOUT any run
# (arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c:2499-2502); pkvm.enabled is set at protected-VM creation. So this test does
# NOT create a vCPU or run. N90 acceptance: memslot register-with-dirty returns -EPERM; no BUG1.

r0 = openat$kvm(0xffffffffffffff9c, &AUTO='/dev/kvm\x00', 0x2, 0x0)
r1 = syz_kvm_setup_protected_vm$arm64(r0, 0x0)
syz_kvm_register_memslot_flags$arm64(r1, 0x1)
close$kvmvm_protected(r1)
